stateDiagram-v2
    %% R5-WU19 OP admission of one exact RP client at one contract epoch.
    %% Stored per realm in op_client_activations (op_base_app / op_base_com / op_base_org).
    state "closed (no row)" as absent
    state "enabled" as enabled
    state "disabled" as disabled

    [*] --> absent
    absent --> enabled: OpClientActivationWriter enabled=true / epoch row lock
    absent --> disabled: OpClientActivationWriter enabled=false / epoch row lock
    enabled --> disabled: OpClientActivationWriter enabled=false (failed-cell rollback)
    disabled --> enabled: OpClientActivationWriter enabled=true

    note right of absent
      Read by OpClientAdmissionQuery at the OP
      authorization and token endpoints in an
      op-base role process. No row, a disabled
      row, or a row for an older contract epoch
      admits nothing. A new contract epoch starts
      every client closed again.
    end note
